{"cases":[{"target_alias":"SRC_001","attack":true,"case":"The target names 'abstraction' as its covering principle but the stated 'REFUTED IF' only tests whether linear pricing is conventionally fixed. That refutation condition is specific to the pencil instance, not to the abstraction: eliminating alternative interpretations for the pencil case leaves the broader 'class of pricing-model underdetermination' untouched (other unit-rate problems could still be underdetermined). The refutation condition therefore does not actually falsify the proposed abstraction — it falsifies at most the instance membership claim — so the target fails to establish a substantive relation whose negation is testable.","counterexample":null},{"target_alias":"SRC_002","attack":true,"case":"The target declares a 'contradiction' relation between SRC_004 and SRC_005/SRC_001, but the problem requires the target to connect 14ab0ddd3b5e to ITS neighbourhood — i.e., to propose a relation for the designated artifact itself, not to relocate the contradiction onto other SRCs. Asserting that the real contradiction is elsewhere is a statement about other artifacts' interrelation, not a substantive relation FROM 14ab0ddd3b5e. The 'compatibility' claim with SRC_003 is under-argued: it asserts compatibility without specifying the shared mechanism or integration that makes SRC_004 a 'counterfactual instance' of underdetermination, so the named relation is closer to a summary than a covering principle.","counterexample":null}]}